@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: stable
+entities: [Comment, CommentReport]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/CommentController.ts
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/CommentResource.ts
+  - app/Policies/CommentPolicy.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-code/fable-5.1", at: 2026-09-29T16:38:02.377Z }
+---
+
+# Hide comments at three reports
+
+## Context
+
+Readers can comment under posts, and no moderator is on call. The community
+has to be able to take a comment off the page by itself, and one bad actor must
+not be able to do that alone.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Any signed-in user can report a comment. `comment_reports` holds one row per
+  report and is unique on (`comment_id`, `user_id`), so a repeated report
+  changes nothing.
+- A comment with `REPORTS_TO_HIDE` (3) or more reports is left out of the post
+  page for every viewer, its author and the post's author included. The count
+  is read from `comment_reports` when the page is built; nothing is stored on
+  the comment.
+- A hidden comment stays in `comments` for later review. A review screen is
+  not part of this decision.
+- A comment is deleted by its author or by the author of the post it is on
+  (`CommentPolicy.delete`). Deleting removes the row and its reports.
+- Comments and reports are deleted by hand (`Comment.purge`), also when their
+  post is deleted. The schema declares `ON DELETE CASCADE`, but a SQLite
+  connection opens with foreign keys off, so the cascade cannot be relied on.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Three accounts acting together can hide any comment; nothing restores it
+  until review tooling exists.
+- Changing the threshold is a one-line change and applies to existing reports
+  at once, because visibility is derived rather than stored.
+- The post page loads every report row of the post's comments to count them.
+  If reports grow large, replace that with a grouped count.
